sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2024-anthrobots-02> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The ability of adult, somatic, genetically wild-type human cells to form a novel functional anatomy with new behaviours shows that the plasticity seen in Xenobots is not restricted to amphibian or embryonic cells, and is a fundamental feature of wild-type cells that needs no direct genetic manipulation to unlock.";
    dc:type "empirical-generalization";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Morphogenetic plasticity is not restricted to amphibian or embryonic cells";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Gumuskaya G, Srivastava P, Cooper BG, Lesser H, Semegran B, Garnier S, Levin M, “Motile Living Biobots Self-Construct from Adult Human Somatic Progenitor Seed Cells”, Advanced science (Weinheim, Baden-Wurttemberg, Germany) (2024), doi:10.1002/advs.202303575; section “Introduction”. Scope: Genetically wild-type cells generally, generalized from adult human airway epithelium and Xenopus embryonic cells"
}
